{"step_index":522,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T10:40:17Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T16:10:17+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T16:10:17+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/brain/296415ce-8ed0-4b1c-b8ba-a547de0a4137/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 78\nTotal Bytes: 3836\nShowing lines 1 to 78\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Walkthrough - NEXUS Prototype Backend\n2: \n3: We have built the backend prototype for the **NEXUS** law enforcement and intelligence analytics platform alongside the React/Vite frontend.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. Accomplishments\n8: \n9: ### Architecture & Ethical Compliance\n10: - **Strictly Synthetic Indian Dataset**: Fictional case `\"Operation Chakravyuh\"` featuring 7 entities (Rahul Verma, Amit Yadav, Priya Singh, Suresh Sharma, Neha Gupta, Scorpio UP14 AB 1234, Canara Bank Account #0492), 10 relationships, 2 possible patterns, and 3 evidence records.\n11: - **Ethical Terminology**: No individual is labeled a \"criminal\". Used neutral language (`subject_of_interest`, `requires human review`, `possible pattern`, `risk indicator`).\n12: - **Database**: Configured lightweight **SQLite** (`sqlite:///./nexus.db`) with SQLAlchemy 2.0 declarative models (`CaseModel`, `EntityModel`, `EvidenceModel`).\n13: - **Graph Engine**: Integrated **NetworkX** to compute topological graph metrics (`degree`, `degree_centrality`, `betweenness_centrality`, `clustering_coefficient`, `density`).\n14: - **Modular Extraction Service**: Architected `extraction_service.py` with `BaseExtractionService` for seamless drop-in upgrades to spaCy NER and Google Gemini API.\n15: - **CORS & Documentation**: Configured CORS for the React frontend (`http://localhost:5173`, `http://localhost:3000`) and interactive Swagger UI (`/docs`) and ReDoc (`/redoc`).\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. API Endpoints Created\n20: \n21: | Method | Path | Summary | Schema / Output |\n22: |:---|:---|:---|:---|\n23: | `GET` | `/health` | Service health check & dataset attribution | `HealthResponse` |\n24: | `GET` | `/api/cases` | List cases with status/priority/search filters | `List[CaseResponse]` |\n25: | `GET` | `/api/cases/{case_id}` | Retrieve case details | `CaseResponse` |\n26: | `POST` | `/api/cases` | Create a new case in registry | `CaseResponse` (201 Created) |\n27: | `GET` | `/api/network/{case_id}` | Case network graph powered by NetworkX | `NetworkGraphData` |\n28: | `GET` | `/api/entities/{entity_id}` | Retrieve subject profile & indicators | `EntityResponse` |\n29: | `GET` | `/api/insights/{case_id}` | AI crime patterns, threat alerts, metrics | `CaseInsightsResponse` |\n30: | `POST` | `/api/upload` | Ingest evidence file (TXT, CSV, JSON only) | `UploadResponse` (201 Created) |\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. Verification & Test Results\n35: \n36: Two automated test suites were built and executed against the FastAPI application:\n37: \n38: ### Phase 1 Test Suite (`backend/tests/test_phase1.py`)\n39: ```\n40: --- RUNNING PHASE 1 ENDPOINT TESTS ---\n41: PASS: test_health_endpoint\n42: PASS: test_list_cases_endpoint (Found 1 cases)\n43: PASS: test_get_case_detail_endpoint\n44: PASS: test_get_case_not_found\n45: PASS: test_create_case_endpoint (Created case ID: case-02)\n46: PASS: test_network_graph_with_networkx (7 nodes, 10 edges, density=0.4762)\n47: PASS: test_get_entity_detail (Verified ent-1 and ent-v1)\n48: PASS: test_get_entity_not_found\n49: PASS: test_insights_endpoint (2 patterns, 3 alerts, 4 metrics)\n50: PASS: test_cors_headers (Allowed origin http://localhost:5173)\n51: --- ALL PHASE 1 TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY! ---\n52: ```\n53: \n54: ### Phase 2 Test Suite (`backend/tests/test_upload.py`)\n55: ```\n56: --- RUNNING UPLOAD ENDPOINT TESTS ---\n57: PASS: test_upload_txt_file (SHA256: 357698f09d32d55c...)\n58: PASS: test_upload_csv_file\n59: PASS: test_upload_json_file\n60: PASS: test_upload_unsupported_file (Properly rejected PDF)\n61: --- ALL UPLOAD TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY! ---\n62: ```\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: ## 4. How to Run the Backend\n67: \n68: To start the FastAPI development server:\n69: ```powershell\n70: cd backend\n71: & \"..\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n72: ```\n73: \n74: Once running:\n75: - **Interactive OpenAPI Documentation (Swagger UI)**: [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs)\n76: - **Alternative Documentation (ReDoc)**: [http://localhost:8000/redoc](http://localhost:8000/redoc)\n77: - **Health Check**: [http://localhost:8000/health](http://localhost:8000/health)\n78: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
